    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0680" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1945-50Intel/pg652"/>

                <head>259. Memorandum From the Director of the Policy Planning Staff (Kennan) to the
                    Under Secretary of State (Lovett)<anchor n="0" xml:id="d259-f1"/></head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1948-02-17">February 17, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                <p>In connection with the decision of the National Security Council regarding
                    psychological warfare operation, I believe it would be advisable if you were to
                    tell Mr. Wisner, in the absence of Mr. Saltzman, that the work of the SANACC
                    Subcommittee on Special Studies and Evaluation<anchor n="1" xml:id="d259-f2"/>
                    should be promptly brought to a conclusion and the subcommittee dissolved.
                    Because of security considerations, Mr. Wisner should not be informed of the
                    reasons lying behind your instructions, but he can be told that this is in
                    response to higher level decision.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">George F. Kennan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d259-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d259-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives and Records Administration, RG 59, Records of the
                    Department of State, Decimal File 1945–49, 101.6/2–1748. Top Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d259-f2" n="1" xml:id="d259-f2-content">
                <p>The designation for the SANACC subcommittee that dealt with psychological
                    warfare.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
